    "number": 66,
    "title": "Expose native power, brightness and saved-scene controls on the controller API",
    "body": "Refs #64. Delivers the accepted general-control definition from hub ADR 0005 (hub #31) for Nanoleaf.\n\n## Problem\n\nThe protected controller only accepted `mode.set`, so the shared BUNNY frontend (hub #153) could not offer Nanoleaf power, brightness or saved-scene controls without an agent session. Controller v1 already carries those commands; the Nanoleaf owner never declared or executed them.\n\n## Resulting behavior\n\n- The capability declaration marks `power` supported, `brightness` supported with the 0 to 100 bound and `scenes` supported with the discovered saved-scene IDs (at most 256). `media`, `zones` and `preview` stay unsupported. The vendored contract archive, schema and all 220 fixture cases are unchanged.\n- `power.set`, `brightness.set` and `scene.activate` pass through the existing request identity, revision, generation, replay, capacity and hold rules and execute as one journaled write each by the installation's single worker. An uncertain write holds the installation like an uncertain mode write; a mode command cancels queued controls as `stale-generation`.\n- Power and brightness are accepted in Work, Quiet and Free. They are overrides: the worker uses the override for every brightness it writes in the current mode (indicators, Quiet steady colors, the blue fallback and the remembered scene when restored while idle), and while desired power is off it writes nothing and keeps tracking tasks. The next explicit mode command from any owner, including the same mode, clears both overrides and reapplies the mode's policy. The remembered scene brightness is never replaced by an override; the scene state records the level the bridge wrote so observation does not adopt it.\n- Scene activation is accepted only when the desired mode is Free. In Work or Quiet it returns the existing `unsupported-capability` failure before any device write, with a replayable receipt. In Free it is one selection write with no polling afterwards; task epochs, comets, unread tracking and reservations are untouched.\n- The worker's existing scene observation discovers scene names; shared v1 carries only opaque epoch-salted IDs. The `nanoleaf.integration/1.0` snapshot gains an additive `scenes` list with the user's Nanoleaf app names (omitted above the 80-character label bound).\n- Snapshots report desired power and brightness as known only while an override is active; pending, last successful send, last outcome and observation stay separate and observation remains unknown.\n\n## Scope and specification\n\n- OpenSpec change `gh-64-native-controls`, synchronized and archived on this branch (`openspec/changes/archive/2026-09-22-gh-64-native-controls`), with `protected-controller-api` and `integration-settings-api` deltas. `npm run openspec -- validate --all --strict` passes (11 items).\n- Docs: `docs/controller-api.md` (new general-controls section), `docs/integration-api.md`, `docs/hub-integration.md`, `bridge/README.md`.\n- Not included: installation, device operations, settings changes, hub #153 UI, hub #155 hardware acceptance.\n\n## Acceptance evidence at `935366db039103e139c01ddbcae2e8a556f687e5`\n\nBase `773d3ca7d97a1fb585baba8e3d9c19c197f337c4` (current `main`), merge-base the same, `git diff 773d3ca...935366d`, worktree clean at commit. Local checks ran on WSL Ubuntu with Python 3.14.4, Node 24.20.0 and jsonschema 4.19.2.\n\n| Criterion | Evidence |\n| --- | --- |\n| AC1 capabilities and fixtures | `test_capabilities_declare_power_brightness_and_scenes_with_constraints`; `test_verified_import_and_all_shared_cases` (220 cases) unchanged and green. Hub companion PR follows the merged revision (see below). |\n| AC2 worker queue rules | `test_admission_replays_power_and_reports_desired_state_before_send`, `test_brightness_executes_once_through_worker_and_governs_work_indicators`, `test_uncertain_control_write_is_held_until_explicit_choice`, `test_mode_command_cancels_queued_control_as_stale_generation`; existing `test_controller_worker` and `test_controller_state` suites green. |\n| AC3 brightness override policy | `test_quiet_idle_override_persists_until_same_mode_quiet_reapplies_ten_percent`, `test_work_idle_override_is_restored_by_same_mode_work_without_reselecting`, `test_free_handoff_clears_override_and_stops_polling`, `test_power_off_suppresses_indicator_writes_and_keeps_tracking`. |\n| AC4 scene gate and one-shot | `test_scene_rejected_in_work_and_quiet_before_any_write`, `test_scene_activates_in_free_with_one_write_and_no_polling`, `test_discovery_is_bounded_named_only_in_extension_and_quiet_between_changes`. |\n| AC5 snapshot separation | desired/pending/lastSuccessfulSend/observation assertions in the admission and brightness tests. |\n| AC6 legacy paths and suites | `python3 scripts/check.py`: 255 tests OK (baseline 243). `npm run test:browser`, `npm run test:prism`, `npm run test:mcp`, `npm run check:workflow`, `npm run test:workflow`: all pass. Tray, installer and hooks are untouched. |\n\nTDD evidence: the 12 tests in `tests/test_controller_controls.py` were run against the unmodified `bridge/` from `773d3ca` before the implementation (8 failures, 3 errors, 1 more failure on the capability test alone) and pass at this head. Two existing assertions changed for the intended contract: brightness is now advertised as supported, and `scene-state.json` gains the `quiet_brightness` key.\n\n## Risk\n\nMedium impact: incorrect writes reach the physical wall. Mitigations are the unchanged hold, replay and cancellation rules, the power gate exemption for a pending mode command, and the recorded written level that keeps overrides out of the remembered brightness. Source tests do not establish visible light output; hub #155 owns hardware acceptance.\n\n## Remaining completion work\n\n- Independent Standards and Specification reviews of this fixed comparison, all configured CI jobs on this head, guarded squash merge, main CI readback.\n- Linked hub companion PR after merge: re-pin `apps/hub/fixtures/nanoleaf-source.json` and `compatibility-nanoleaf-source.json` to the merged revision, update the compatibility record and record this delivery in `docs/work-guide/updates.md`. Its URL and status will be recorded here. Guide synchronization is pending until it merges; public guide publication is separate and not requested.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
